# org-target: docs/10-19-design/10-architecture/10.23-native-aitia-backpressure-content-review.org::#native-aitia-backpressure-review
# render-layout: elk; theme: 0; pad: 24; timeout: 30
direction: down
library: "Existing Library / accepted Core baseline\nParent obligations -> Rust specialization\nReal source + Cargo.lock + QNT / Lean / Rust results"
ascent: "Existing ASCENT Evidence DSL\n22 records / 9 historical query cuts / 7 exchanges\nKeep original T/V identity and counters"
profile: "Scenario Review Profile\nLocal coding method v1 / SWE-061/p1\nWorker-owned or caller-owned selection\nDeclared class a; institutional authority pending"
audit: "Independent content audit\nAccepted observation equality + raw event oracle\nFinite BFS + counter trace + integer budget\nUnique dependency closure; preserve historical cuts"
packet: "Actual review packet bytes\nPolicy + selection + subject / revision / scope\nReport + consumer sources + dependency digests\nNative criterion artifact digest"
aitia: "Native Aitia + Core verification\nApplicability / content request snapshots\nGenuine receipts; expiry / revocation / clone rejection\nNo restored method issuer from JSON"
reuse: "Reuse stable T/V content\nCheck complete footprint at each boundary\nNew revision -> new packet and A receipts\nNo repeated tool run or oracle recomputation within one review"
gate: "Native stage gate\nContext missing -> pending\nContent missing -> pending\nVerified safe method -> bounded admission"
block: "Actual selected M06 failure\nTruthfully verified failure still blocks\nExplicit rebase carries unresolved failure\nCurrent pass cannot override it"
open: "Open authority boundaries\nInstitutional classification / global history\nBounded native dispositions: follow-up 90.79\nHuman approval / atomic use authorization\nNo release or performance claim"
library -> ascent -> audit
profile -> audit -> packet -> aitia -> gate
aitia -> reuse -> gate
ascent -> block -> gate: "failure priority"
gate -> open
